# UI: responsive layout and skeletons

- Build every screen so it works on phone, tablet, and desktop. Stack controls on small screens, use the existing sidebar below `lg` and the full layout from `lg` up. Do not add a layout that only fits a wide desktop.
- While data or an action is loading, show a skeleton placeholder from `frontend/src/components/Skeleton.tsx`. Do not show the words Loading, Saving, Preparing, Signing in, Deleting, Submitting, Working, or Applying.
- Page loads use `DashboardSkeleton`, `TableSkeleton`, `CardGridSkeleton`, or `AppBootSkeleton`. In-progress buttons use `BusyLabel`. Document previews use `PdfSkeleton`.
